            <div xml:id="d69">

                <pb facs="0164" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg60"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3634: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-25T17:00:00+08:00">January 25, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Foreign members of Shanghai Municipal Council including Japanese held a meeting
                    this morning to determine whether a state of emergency exists and the decision
                    was in the negative for the time being. I learn from thoroughly reliable source
                    that Japanese Consul General has promised that reply from Mayor to Japanese
                    demands given in my January 25, 2 p.m., will be given to Council 24 hours in
                    advance of any Japanese action. Reply is expected this afternoon.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
